'''Glaro''' and '''Twabo''' are two largely [[mutually intelligible]] dialects of the [[Wèè languages]] which are divergent other. ''[[Ethnologue]]'' reports that Twabo (but not Glaro) has slight intelligibility with some dialects of [[Eastern Krahn language|Eastern Krahn]].

